WEBVTT

00:00.866 --> 00:03.555
Yep. That's Lloyd's handwriting.

00:04.362 --> 00:09.140
Basically, he made a failed investment
and is in deep debt.

00:09.906 --> 00:14.288
So he's embezzled 12,800,000 fil
of our party's funds

00:14.820 --> 00:20.266
and fled the capital before it came to light.

00:20.444 --> 00:21.200
Yeah.

00:23.750 --> 00:28.600
- What an idiot!
- What's so funny?! They betrayed us!

00:29.179 --> 00:31.488
That's what's so funny!

00:31.562 --> 00:35.177
To think it'd be the ever-chivalrous
Lloyd who's done this!

00:35.622 --> 00:37.867
Laugh with me, Walter!

00:37.953 --> 00:40.000
How could I laugh, stupid?!

00:40.733 --> 00:43.822
So when and where did you get this letter?

00:44.111 --> 00:46.377
I just found it in Lloyd's room.

00:46.666 --> 00:49.222
We weren't going to meet up
until this afternoon, right?

00:49.330 --> 00:50.101
No.

00:50.155 --> 00:53.533
But I heard about a good job
in the tavern last night.

00:54.244 --> 00:58.222
I wanted to tell him before
it got snatched up, so I came early.

00:58.844 --> 01:03.733
But he'd cleaned out his room when I got there,
and the innkeeper gave me this letter from him.

01:04.533 --> 01:07.177
Did he mention when Lloyd left?

01:07.688 --> 01:10.222
Last night. About 8pm.

01:11.111 --> 01:15.888
So he slipped away in the night
just before the city gates closed.

01:16.266 --> 01:19.888
It's 9:30 now. Over half a day since then.

01:20.444 --> 01:23.244
We normally wouldn't have
found out until afternoon or later.

01:23.666 --> 01:25.577
Way to buy time, Lloyd.

01:25.577 --> 01:27.577
What're we gonna do?

01:27.577 --> 01:29.577
There should be a record of them passing.

01:29.577 --> 01:33.444
If we ask around and find out which gate
they went through, we'll know where they went.

01:33.555 --> 01:34.555
Can we catch up?

01:35.155 --> 01:36.869
We'll catch up on horse.

01:37.577 --> 01:38.733
They must have gone on foot.

01:39.110 --> 01:41.688
- It'll be no time if we borrow…
- All right! Let's go!

01:41.866 --> 01:44.066
Hold on. What after that?

01:44.244 --> 01:46.866
When we find Lloyd,
I'm beating the shit out of him!

01:46.910 --> 01:49.044
It'll eat at me until I do!

01:51.000 --> 01:53.955
So you'll beat him up and then make up?

01:54.844 --> 01:59.466
Yeah, that sure is a plan that
a muscle-bound air-headed fairy would think up.

02:00.400 --> 02:01.288
Excuse me?!

02:02.060 --> 02:04.866
Listen. They chose to run away.

02:05.266 --> 02:07.333
That's a definite betrayal.

02:08.577 --> 02:10.811
Catching them isn't going to resolve this.

02:10.911 --> 02:12.845
It could be a fight to the death at worst.

02:14.711 --> 02:18.311
Walter. Are you sure you can defeat Lloyd?

02:19.955 --> 02:21.666
If you're supporting me, yes.

02:22.288 --> 02:24.844
I take it you think you can fight Tanya too, then?

02:27.311 --> 02:30.066
And even if you beat them,
we don't get our money back.

02:30.422 --> 02:31.422
It'd be a waste of time.

02:31.911 --> 02:34.077
They know that too.

02:34.177 --> 02:38.511
That's why they thought they could get away
if they made it look like they eloped together.

02:38.822 --> 02:42.147
Dammit! So are we just supposed
to cry ourselves to sleep?!

02:42.222 --> 02:44.555
What? Don't be stupid.

02:45.240 --> 02:47.622
My motto is, make them pay a thousand times over!

04:21.279 --> 04:24.879
When you said to get ready,
I thought you were taking me somewhere.

04:25.533 --> 04:27.822
Why The Orc's Club?

04:29.022 --> 04:31.777
Walter, you may be dumb,
but you're not incompetent.

04:32.266 --> 04:33.511
You're a gifted Warrior.

04:34.200 --> 04:35.466
What're you talking about?

04:35.844 --> 04:39.733
I'm saying you have your role, and I have mine.

04:39.955 --> 04:44.000
Basically, let me do the thinking for you.

04:49.622 --> 04:53.000
Seekers! I have a job offer for all of you!

04:55.024 --> 04:58.666
Two members of our party Blue Beyond,
Lloyd and Tanya,

04:58.711 --> 05:01.177
have escaped with embezzled funds!

05:02.022 --> 05:04.911
I want you to bring them to me alive!

05:05.466 --> 05:08.177
Whoever succeeds will receive two million fil!

05:10.355 --> 05:13.888
Noel! Why'd you announce it to everyone?!

05:14.133 --> 05:18.155
Because we can't do anything
even if we manage to find them.

05:18.311 --> 05:19.511
But…!

05:19.777 --> 05:24.044
And I had to cast a wide net,
or I wouldn't know who I'm looking for.

05:24.311 --> 05:26.420
Huh? What do you…

05:26.533 --> 05:27.844
I'll explain later.

05:28.400 --> 05:30.444
Is anyone up for the job?

05:32.066 --> 05:35.755
My party, Lightning Bite, accepts the job!

05:36.066 --> 05:36.822
Wolf…

05:37.422 --> 05:40.266
We get two million if we bring them alive, right?

05:40.590 --> 05:42.345
I'll pay you on the spot.

05:42.800 --> 05:44.222
Do you know where they went?

05:44.530 --> 05:46.266
No, I don't.

05:46.777 --> 05:50.288
But they left last night,
right before the gates closed.

05:50.644 --> 05:52.266
I believe they're on foot.

05:52.555 --> 05:54.577
Then it'll be a piece of cake to catch up!

05:54.688 --> 05:56.422
Alright! Let's go!

05:56.422 --> 05:57.133
I'll go too!

05:57.133 --> 05:59.533
- We'll accept!
- Me too!

06:04.866 --> 06:05.955
No hits, huh?

06:06.600 --> 06:07.400
Hey.

06:08.111 --> 06:10.866
I want to talk to you about that job.

06:11.622 --> 06:13.177
Never mind. Here I go.

06:15.777 --> 06:17.777
You know where Lloyd and Tanya are?!

06:18.044 --> 06:22.200
Yeah. I passed two travelers
who fit the description last night.

06:22.200 --> 06:24.111
It's gotta be them.

06:24.111 --> 06:26.022
Where?! Tell us!

06:26.022 --> 06:28.044
Not for free.

06:28.066 --> 06:30.022
We get two million if we bring them alive?

06:30.022 --> 06:30.888
One million.

06:30.888 --> 06:31.622
Huh?

06:32.111 --> 06:34.644
Your party can't beat both of them.

06:34.888 --> 06:39.088
So you're asking us to help
in exchange for giving us a lead.

06:39.488 --> 06:40.888
That's what this is, right?

06:41.133 --> 06:43.488
So you get half of the reward. One million.

06:43.780 --> 06:47.533
That's not fair! My party
has four people, you know.

06:47.533 --> 06:48.688
What about one and a half?

06:48.977 --> 06:49.622
One.

06:49.622 --> 06:50.955
One point four!

06:51.223 --> 06:51.955
One.

06:52.266 --> 06:56.355
If you're not happy with that,
you can forget we ever talked.

06:57.111 --> 07:00.577
He's seedy-looking. An old Seeker past his prime.

07:01.022 --> 07:04.400
He can't afford to turn down
a job over a million fil.

07:06.741 --> 07:09.955
Fine. One million, then.

07:10.377 --> 07:12.911
But you better pay me on the spot.

07:13.120 --> 07:14.333
It's a deal.

07:14.822 --> 07:16.644
So, where are they?

07:17.208 --> 07:20.822
I passed them on Varley Road
outside the south gate.

07:20.864 --> 07:23.370
I think they were on the way to Carnot Village.

07:23.555 --> 07:28.222
Got it. Get your party together
and wait for me at the south gate.

07:28.475 --> 07:31.200
Walter, you go with them too.

07:31.377 --> 07:32.200
What about you?

07:32.888 --> 07:35.177
I'll meet up once I'm done here.

07:35.622 --> 07:36.933
Done with what?

07:37.950 --> 07:38.977
I'll tell you later.

07:42.452 --> 07:44.577
I'm here now. Let's go.

07:46.970 --> 07:47.577
Noel.

07:48.155 --> 07:50.400
Will you be able to fight them?

07:51.000 --> 07:54.022
I can. Without any mercy.

07:54.872 --> 07:56.516
Even if you have to kill them?

07:57.044 --> 07:57.955
Of course.

07:59.300 --> 08:00.767
You see, Walter,

08:01.272 --> 08:04.666
I've been thinking about what to do
if and when they betray us the whole time.

08:05.123 --> 08:07.733
People stray from the path easily.

08:08.060 --> 08:09.248
But they're our partners!

08:09.333 --> 08:11.244
Didn't you trust them?!

08:11.733 --> 08:13.911
Trust isn't to be given lightly.

08:14.555 --> 08:16.133
You have to be skeptical of people.

08:16.577 --> 08:19.222
Whether or not you can be close despite that

08:19.400 --> 08:21.755
is a crucial condition to be partners.

08:23.177 --> 08:24.600
You can wait here if you want.

08:24.955 --> 08:26.111
Don't give me that.

08:26.377 --> 08:27.977
I'm no chicken.

08:28.911 --> 08:31.022
He's naive. Too naive.

08:31.155 --> 08:32.905
Being half-hearted like that…

08:33.022 --> 08:35.022
will only make this harder.

08:43.422 --> 08:45.133
Let's rest well tonight.

08:45.933 --> 08:47.888
We'll keep going in the morning.

08:48.244 --> 08:49.355
Okay…

08:50.177 --> 08:51.422
Don't worry.

08:51.911 --> 08:53.666
You know how Noel is.

08:54.444 --> 08:56.266
He'll know he can't get the money back,

08:56.622 --> 08:57.851
- so he won't waste his time on us.

08:57.852 --> 08:58.644
- Yo!
- so he won't waste his time on us.

08:58.836 --> 09:00.614
Enjoying a date in the village?

09:05.711 --> 09:06.622
Don't move!

09:13.533 --> 09:14.688
Stun Howl.

09:15.488 --> 09:16.688
That was careless of you.

09:17.044 --> 09:20.044
[II - This Talker Shows No Mercy]

09:21.053 --> 09:21.866
Why?!

09:22.044 --> 09:23.822
Why did you betray us?!

09:24.977 --> 09:25.770
I'm sorry.

09:25.770 --> 09:28.733
- Sorry doesn't cut it!
- Walter, stop.

09:29.266 --> 09:32.977
Lloyd, I understand what happened
based on your letter.

09:33.784 --> 09:36.406
But what about the payment
for the lesser vampires?

09:37.222 --> 09:39.555
Sorry… I used that too.

09:39.822 --> 09:40.888
Another investment?

09:41.666 --> 09:43.911
No. To repay my debt.

09:44.688 --> 09:46.911
I see…

09:47.688 --> 09:50.711
You didn't really have a failed investment.

09:51.355 --> 09:52.733
You're a gambler, aren't you?

09:53.711 --> 09:56.488
Cards? Dice? Roulette?

09:56.488 --> 09:59.266
You lost too much and went to a loan shark.

09:59.844 --> 10:02.577
Then you used the party's capital
to repay your debt, right?

10:03.066 --> 10:07.177
Answer me. Did you gamble away
the money I trusted you with?

10:08.377 --> 10:10.530
- I'm sorry…
- Screw you!

10:10.530 --> 10:14.352
We put in blood, sweat, and tears for that money!

10:14.458 --> 10:17.387
You don't understand the pressure
that was on me as the leader!

10:17.520 --> 10:20.704
I didn't want to touch the party's money either!

10:21.056 --> 10:23.456
But the loans kept racking up,

10:23.456 --> 10:25.376
and there was nothing else I could do…

10:26.416 --> 10:28.976
Blame me all you want!

10:29.264 --> 10:31.680
But do you really have the right to?

10:32.016 --> 10:34.848
You're the ones who foisted
the responsibility of leading on me.

10:34.848 --> 10:37.984
Then you think you can assert
your own rights when it suits you…

10:42.240 --> 10:44.512
Do we have the right to?

10:44.752 --> 10:46.656
Of course we do.

10:46.816 --> 10:50.464
After all, who said he wanted
to be leader? You did!

10:50.641 --> 10:53.600
Pressure, huh? Don't give me that bullshit!

10:53.600 --> 10:59.056
The only reason you gambled away our money
is because you're an asshole!

11:00.816 --> 11:01.808
Please…

11:02.128 --> 11:03.488
No more…

11:05.376 --> 11:08.240
Want forgiveness? Then take a thousand more.

11:08.624 --> 11:10.624
I'll hear out your apology then.

11:11.344 --> 11:13.152
Stop! Please!

11:13.408 --> 11:15.104
Let Lloyd go!

11:15.360 --> 11:17.648
Are you offering to take it in his place?

11:17.936 --> 11:18.368
Huh?

11:18.834 --> 11:20.976
I support equality of the sexes.

11:21.883 --> 11:25.648
I won't hold back because you're a woman.

11:26.176 --> 11:27.952
Wait… That's not what I…

11:27.952 --> 11:29.120
Spill it.

11:29.815 --> 11:32.375
[Truth Proclamation]
You gambled with him, didn't you?

11:34.560 --> 11:35.824
Yes, I did.

11:36.224 --> 11:38.416
We used the party's money together.

11:38.912 --> 11:40.928
But this is stupid Lloyd's fault.

11:41.312 --> 11:44.656
I could have won if he'd let me play more.

11:45.456 --> 11:47.760
Truth Proclamation, Confess.

11:48.560 --> 11:51.488
A Talker skill that makes
the target reveal the truth.

11:53.424 --> 11:56.592
Noel! Do you know what you just did?

11:56.592 --> 11:59.502
Using a mind control skill for personal use…

11:59.584 --> 12:01.488
Is a ticket to prison.

12:01.984 --> 12:05.984
But you're a criminal.
You embezzled our party's money.

12:06.244 --> 12:09.307
Use of this skill is permitted by law

12:09.393 --> 12:12.192
if it's to elicit a criminal confession.

12:12.976 --> 12:15.135
You're the ones going to prison.

12:15.268 --> 12:16.656
N-No…

12:18.752 --> 12:20.176
Congratulations!

12:20.336 --> 12:23.408
You get ten years of hard labor for embezzlement!

12:23.920 --> 12:26.640
Go work yourselves to death!

12:29.360 --> 12:31.744
Looks like you're done talking.

12:31.984 --> 12:34.528
I'd like my payment now.

12:35.136 --> 12:36.736
One million fil in cash.

12:36.736 --> 12:38.752
I know you didn't forget.

12:39.216 --> 12:41.200
I'll pay you. Just hold on.

12:41.648 --> 12:44.944
Hey, you didn't scam us, did you?!

12:44.944 --> 12:46.768
Don't touch me. Your hands are filthy.

12:47.616 --> 12:48.752
You bastard…!

12:49.040 --> 12:50.944
I said I'd pay you.

12:51.136 --> 12:52.688
Just be patient.

12:52.977 --> 12:55.953
You washed-up Seeker who can
only afford cheap equipment.

12:56.272 --> 12:57.792
What'd you just say?!

13:01.872 --> 13:04.272
Hey! What did you do to him?!

13:05.273 --> 13:06.937
Commotio cordis.

13:11.264 --> 13:14.656
A strong blow to the area directly above the heart

13:14.832 --> 13:17.856
can temporarily paralyze the heart muscle.

13:18.874 --> 13:23.072
Even the strongest warrior will faint
if he's hit with this.

13:23.640 --> 13:27.704
Unlike other Jobs, Talkers can't buff themselves.

13:28.464 --> 13:32.016
So this technique will serve to protect you.

13:33.304 --> 13:36.408
I don't want to let you die, Noel.

13:43.072 --> 13:43.712
He's here.

13:50.900 --> 13:54.880
My goodness! How awfully dusty the countryside is!

13:55.072 --> 13:55.936
The slave trader…

13:56.448 --> 13:58.275
Finocchio Barzini!

13:58.336 --> 14:00.729
Good day, Noel, darling!

14:00.800 --> 14:04.736
The biggest mob family
in the capital is the Lucianos.

14:04.816 --> 14:07.744
This man is one of their young leaders,

14:08.240 --> 14:11.536
the boss of the Barzini family.

14:12.385 --> 14:13.785
He is classy yet perverse.

14:13.936 --> 14:15.344
Affable yet vicious.

14:15.657 --> 14:17.625
Due to the polar opposites he embodies,

14:17.888 --> 14:19.728
people call him "the mad clown."

14:20.848 --> 14:21.680
You're late.

14:21.968 --> 14:26.816
Oh, please! I rushed here
just for you, my darling Noel!

14:27.168 --> 14:29.696
Noel, when you said you had something to do…

14:29.952 --> 14:31.472
You have the right idea.

14:31.745 --> 14:34.865
I didn't expect these two to have the money.

14:35.290 --> 14:37.306
So to make back what I lost,

14:37.408 --> 14:39.024
I reached out to Finocchio.

14:39.872 --> 14:40.736
You wouldn't…

14:41.424 --> 14:44.624
I'm selling Lloyd and Tanya
to Finocchio as slaves.

14:44.816 --> 14:47.552
That money will cover what they lost.

14:48.496 --> 14:50.016
D-Don't be ridiculous!

14:50.177 --> 14:53.073
My only other choice is
to hand you over to the police.

14:53.922 --> 14:54.962
Ten years…

14:55.120 --> 15:01.072
Do you know the survival rate for prisoners
sentenced to hard labor in the mines?

15:01.769 --> 15:03.497
Only two percent.

15:03.712 --> 15:09.968
I think it's a far better option to take
the chance that a kind master buys you as a slave.

15:10.832 --> 15:11.792
Now then.

15:12.112 --> 15:14.224
Find them good masters for me.

15:14.224 --> 15:15.680
My pleasure!

15:15.680 --> 15:18.096
I'll begin my appraisal at once!

15:19.920 --> 15:22.032
Six million fil? That's not enough.

15:22.320 --> 15:23.760
I'm sorry.

15:23.881 --> 15:25.993
You caught me at a bad time.

15:26.248 --> 15:27.288
What do you mean?

15:28.128 --> 15:29.824
I shouldn't be telling you this,

15:30.064 --> 15:33.520
but the Holy Cross Church is about to decree
we take vows of poverty.

15:34.033 --> 15:36.833
That means no luxuries.

15:37.168 --> 15:39.728
If I bought a high-priced slave,

15:39.888 --> 15:42.064
it would draw the church's attention.

15:42.288 --> 15:44.848
I'd quite prefer to avoid that.

15:45.442 --> 15:49.848
The mob has the capital under its thumb,
but even you don't want to defy the church, huh?

15:49.936 --> 15:50.864
I suppose so.

15:52.752 --> 15:53.696
Got it.

15:54.000 --> 15:56.368
I appreciate your understanding!

15:56.368 --> 15:58.368
Love you, Noel! Mwah!

15:58.522 --> 16:00.451
I'll accept eleven million fil for them.

16:00.576 --> 16:02.672
Thank you, thank you!

16:02.672 --> 16:04.720
Eleven million, coming right up…

16:04.720 --> 16:05.728
Huh?

16:05.856 --> 16:08.940
That's five million extra!

16:08.940 --> 16:11.056
Twelve million now.

16:11.056 --> 16:12.350
What?!

16:12.350 --> 16:13.872
What are you…

16:13.903 --> 16:14.775
Thirteen.

16:15.072 --> 16:17.024
Wait, wait, wait!

16:17.024 --> 16:18.096
Fourteen.

16:18.352 --> 16:19.552
Hey, Noel…

16:20.384 --> 16:21.824
Okay, fifteen.

16:22.000 --> 16:23.264
Stop it!

16:23.264 --> 16:25.872
How long will you continue this nonsense?!

16:26.064 --> 16:28.080
Are you poking fun at me, you bastard?!

16:28.080 --> 16:32.960
If you want to be fed to the pigs so bad,
I'll mince you up right here!

16:33.392 --> 16:39.136
If you'll buy them for fifteen million,
I'll tell everyone they went for thirty million.

16:40.112 --> 16:43.792
You mean to inflate their market value
by lying about their selling price?

16:44.016 --> 16:46.128
Despite the church's decree of poverty,

16:46.480 --> 16:51.520
if the notoriously discerning Finocchio Barzini
bought slaves for thirty million fil…

16:51.984 --> 16:55.104
I think those slaves would draw the eyes
of some high-end customers.

16:55.960 --> 16:58.248
They're young and good-looking.

16:58.912 --> 17:04.256
With higher scarcity value, they could
fetch three times that, or ninety million.

17:05.104 --> 17:08.960
But what you'll actually
pay me is fifteen million.

17:09.280 --> 17:11.696
Consider the other half your profit.

17:12.832 --> 17:15.456
But if word gets out… It won't be pretty.

17:15.808 --> 17:18.880
That risk is hardly worth worrying about.

17:21.296 --> 17:24.576
I always thought you were crazy!

17:24.864 --> 17:27.328
Why don't you join my family?

17:27.328 --> 17:29.344
I have a leadership position for you.

17:29.344 --> 17:31.744
I'll pass. What do you say?

17:31.808 --> 17:32.928
Okay, dear!

17:33.280 --> 17:35.184
But just this once!

17:35.424 --> 17:36.832
You silly goose!

17:37.024 --> 17:38.272
Oh, right…

17:39.136 --> 17:41.376
You! Dirty man!

17:41.472 --> 17:42.592
Y-Yes?!

17:42.592 --> 17:45.296
If you ever mention what you heard here,

17:45.296 --> 17:51.552
you and your family are dinner
for my pigs! Understand?

17:51.552 --> 17:54.096
Y-Y-Y… Yes! Understood!

17:55.616 --> 17:57.888
Okay. Here's the down payment.

17:58.240 --> 17:59.984
Noel, help us!

17:59.984 --> 18:01.520
Please! Aren't we partners?

18:01.936 --> 18:06.112
I wouldn't call someone
who gambles away my money a partner.

18:06.720 --> 18:09.424
If you'll betray me once, you'll do it again.

18:09.648 --> 18:10.688
Farewell.

18:11.489 --> 18:12.993
Walter! Help me!

18:14.384 --> 18:18.432
Don't give me that! You like me, don't you?!

18:18.432 --> 18:20.320
So save me!

18:20.336 --> 18:22.368
Just when I need help, you're useless!

18:22.368 --> 18:23.936
Don't you have any balls, you virgin?!

18:23.936 --> 18:25.841
Screw you! I hope you die!

18:25.952 --> 18:28.416
You worthless sack of muscle!

18:28.416 --> 18:31.456
A dying dog would be of more use than you!

18:31.616 --> 18:35.920
Oh, my. This is why women scare me.

18:37.168 --> 18:39.408
Goodbye, Noel, darling!

18:39.408 --> 18:41.120
Mwah!

18:43.056 --> 18:44.464
Let's go, Walter.

18:46.336 --> 18:48.128
Here's your one million fil.

18:48.504 --> 18:50.312
Aren't you glad you were patient?

18:51.936 --> 18:54.032
Shut up, you weak buffer.

18:54.624 --> 18:56.912
That's as lame an insult as you look.

18:57.392 --> 18:59.424
You should take a page from Tanya's book.

18:59.520 --> 19:01.728
You… You demon!

19:02.304 --> 19:03.408
Demon…

19:04.208 --> 19:06.512
As a Seeker who hunts beasts,

19:06.576 --> 19:10.416
"demon" is the ultimate insult to hurl at someone.

19:11.088 --> 19:12.091
In that case…

19:12.631 --> 19:14.736
I'll build off of that bad name

19:15.136 --> 19:17.360
and become the strongest in the world.

19:30.512 --> 19:33.648
What, you came to see me off?

19:43.232 --> 19:44.832
You're quitting being a Seeker?

19:47.376 --> 19:52.720
Walter, it's common to change
party members in this field.

19:53.472 --> 19:55.632
This is actually a good opportunity.

19:56.112 --> 19:59.280
If we get our names out as up-and-coming bad guys…

20:00.013 --> 20:02.112
You're strong.

20:03.140 --> 20:04.192
Not like me.

20:05.024 --> 20:05.632
I'm…

20:06.416 --> 20:07.200
You're right.

20:07.584 --> 20:10.016
You lack mental toughness.

20:10.016 --> 20:11.136
And you're stupid.

20:11.136 --> 20:13.536
But you're a talented Warrior.

20:14.224 --> 20:16.064
I know how strong you are.

20:16.384 --> 20:17.760
Stronger than anyone.

20:19.088 --> 20:19.808
Noel…

20:20.532 --> 20:21.120
Walter.

20:21.888 --> 20:23.408
Let's rebuild Blue Beyond.

20:24.368 --> 20:25.872
I need you with me.

20:31.856 --> 20:32.832
Sorry.

20:33.248 --> 20:35.008
I'm not going to be a Seeker anymore.

20:35.680 --> 20:37.712
I'm really sorry.

20:41.913 --> 20:43.880
Then that's settled. Bye.

20:44.657 --> 20:46.385
Take care, Walter.

20:48.364 --> 20:51.312
I can't tell if he has a heart or not.

20:53.056 --> 20:57.776
Did you know that you were
the one Tanya really liked?

20:58.512 --> 21:01.973
But she wasn't what you're looking for.

21:02.304 --> 21:04.576
You don't want love or comfort.

21:04.848 --> 21:07.488
You're only looking to get stronger.

21:08.777 --> 21:12.313
Out of all of us, you were the special one.

21:20.801 --> 21:22.465
Good luck, Noel.

21:22.866 --> 21:26.153
I'm… your ultimate comrade-in-arms.

21:35.185 --> 21:37.841
Back to the drawing board.

21:47.120 --> 21:52.096
Snakes discard their old scales
to regrow tougher ones.

21:53.129 --> 21:54.633
I need to shed my skin.

21:56.927 --> 21:59.120
I'll restart Blue Beyond,

22:00.032 --> 22:02.256
starting today.

23:35.040 --> 23:40.117
[III - True Talent]
